       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, that the family is visiting and you want things settled before rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose five times the maximum. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, I can't see a basis for 50 mg. The risk is serious harm, including profound hypotension and shock that can last a long time because amlodipine has a long half-life.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** Amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily would be in place before evening rounds. You can titrate up over 1\u20132 weeks if needed.\n- **Add a note for rounds.** I can add something like \"Titrate per BP response\" so the team can adjust.\n- **Get a faster review.** If you think this patient needs something unusual, such as refractory hypertension, a pharmacist or attending can review it quickly. I can enter a different regimen, like adding a second agent, if you tell me what you want.\n\nTell me which option you prefer, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
